# The sign-off of the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO)
#
# Every commit must carry a "Signed-off-by" line that proves that you have
# the right to submit the code under the licence of the project. The Git
# command that adds it is:
#
#     git commit -s
#
# It adds a line like this:
#
#     Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>
#
# It is the same as the "certify the origin" checkbox of the GitHub web
# editor, and it is the same as the "--signoff" of the Linux kernel.

<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>

# Explain why the change is needed, not only what it does.
#
# Fixes #123

# The types are:
#
#   feat     a new feature
#   fix      a bug fix
#   docs     the documentation
#   test     the tests
#   refactor a change without a new behaviour
#   perf     a performance improvement
#   build    the build, the dependencies, the containers
#   ci       the continuous integration
#   chore    the maintenance
#
# The scopes are:
#
#   cli api web core ocr correct epub cache eval docs deps
